window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b369-b62fde2d5e7e3da9.json"]={sha256:"b62fde2d5e7e3da98a818d7849e0a8e37165df5c24b4e614efcf95e66b6e6a1c",value:{"id":"b369","title":"列車自動監督系統","titleEn":"Automatic train supervision systems","category":"rail","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課聚焦列車監督排程與旅客資訊的一致性。從班距監督與瓶頸建立物理或資訊邊界，接著把旅客服務需求累積與營運異常警報排序連成可驗證的介面，最後以監督整合重播計畫整理證據。學徒逐一完成機制推導、數值算例、失效辨識及參數實驗，所有練習限定在離線模型或隔離教具，保留假設與量測的不確定度。","summaryEn":"This course studies consistency of train supervision scheduling and passenger information. Start with headway supervision and bottlenecks to define physical or information boundaries, connect accumulation of passenger service demand with ordering operational alarms as verifiable interfaces, and organize evidence through supervision integration replay plan. Each unit develops a mechanism, numerical example, failure diagnosis and parameter experiment in an offline model or isolated teaching rig, retaining assumptions and measurement uncertainty.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、軌道進入、牽引供電隔離或列車營運許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, track-access, traction-power isolation or train-operation permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"rail-control","subcategoryTitle":"號誌與營運控制","subcategoryTitleEn":"Signalling and operational control","learningTrack":"rail","learningSubdiscipline":"rail-control","learningTags":["rail","rail-control","control"],"architectureFamily":"rail-control","architectureNodes":[["列車回報","Train reports"],["狀態彙整","State aggregation"],["排程資源","Schedule resources"],["旅客資訊","Passenger information"],["事件紀錄","Event log"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"rail-control","labels":["列車回報","狀態彙整","排程資源","旅客資訊","事件紀錄"],"labelsEn":["Train reports","State aggregation","Schedule resources","Passenger information","Event log"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創整合工作單，所有輸入均為教學假設而非代表工程實測：先研究班距監督與瓶頸。原創假想教學輸入：列車占用長度 L=180 m；假想防護距離 S=420 m；等速速度 v=15 m/s；附加處理時間 td=20 s。公式 y=(L+S)/v+td，代入得 y=60 s。邊界：等速單一資源的概念下界，不是任何號誌系統的實際最小班距。敏感度只改 S=420 至 462 m，輸出變為 62.8 s；離散計數採整數變化。再獨立研究時刻偏差吸收：原創假想教學輸入：排定間隔 scheduled=140 s；資源占用 occupied=110 s；入侵延誤 delay=18 s。公式 y=scheduled-occupied-delay，代入得 y=12 s。邊界：單一衝突資源與確定延誤，未求解整個網路的隨機時刻最佳化。兩個結果不能因同一課程就任意相加，必須先確認單位、因果順序及共同邊界。本單元以月台占用和區間追蹤兩個資源比較班距，先找瓶頸再討論監督系統可調整的空間。最後提出一項量測能區分模型假設失效與儀器偏差，將輸入表、重算結果和適用限制一併交付。","textEn":"Original integrated worksheet; every input is a teaching assumption rather than a measurement from a reference project. First investigate headway supervision and bottlenecks. Original hypothetical teaching inputs: occupied train length L=180 m; hypothetical protected distance S=420 m; constant speed v=15 m/s; additional processing time td=20 s. Formula y=(L+S)/v+td gives y=60 s. Boundary: Conceptual lower bound for one resource at constant speed, not an operating minimum for any signalling system. For sensitivity, change only S=420 to 462 m; the output becomes 62.8 s. Discrete counts use whole-number steps. Independently investigate absorbing timetable deviation: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: scheduled interval scheduled=140 s; resource occupation occupied=110 s; incoming delay delay=18 s. Formula y=scheduled-occupied-delay gives y=12 s. Boundary: One conflicting resource and a deterministic delay; no stochastic network-wide timetable optimization is implied. Results cannot be added merely because they belong to the same course: check units, causal sequence and shared boundaries first. Compare platform occupation and open-line following as separate headway resources, identifying the bottleneck before considering what supervision can adjust. Propose one measurement distinguishing a failed model assumption from instrument bias, and deliver the input table, recomputed results and applicability limits together.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":16,"enrichmentVersion":16,"stages":[{"id":"b369-v16-s1","title":"班距監督與瓶頸與時刻偏差吸收","titleEn":"Headway supervision and bottlenecks & Absorbing timetable deviation","description":"本階段聚焦「班距監督與瓶頸」與「時刻偏差吸收」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Headway supervision and bottlenecks\" and \"Absorbing timetable deviation\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b369-v16-01","title":"班距監督與瓶頸：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Headway supervision and bottlenecks: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「班距監督與瓶頸」如何影響列車自動監督系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Headway supervision and bottlenecks” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Automatic train supervision systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元以月台占用和區間追蹤兩個資源比較班距，先找瓶頸再討論監督系統可調整的空間。班距是時間資源問題，不能僅用兩車車頭距離判斷。列車長度、防護距離與釋放時間會共同占用線路；車站停靠、路口衝突或折返可能比區間運轉更先成為瓶頸，所以縮小單一間隔不等於全線增能。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：等速單一資源的概念下界，不是任何號誌系統的實際最小班距。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「班距監督與瓶頸」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Compare platform occupation and open-line following as separate headway resources, identifying the bottleneck before considering what supervision can adjust. Headway is a time-resource problem, not merely a distance between train fronts. Train length, protected separation and release time occupy the route together. Dwell, conflicting junctions or terminal reversals can dominate capacity before open-line running does, so reducing one interval need not raise line throughput. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Conceptual lower bound for one resource at constant speed, not an operating minimum for any signalling system. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Headway supervision and bottlenecks” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：列車占用長度 L=180 m；假想防護距離 S=420 m；等速速度 v=15 m/s；附加處理時間 td=20 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: occupied train length L=180 m; hypothetical protected distance S=420 m; constant speed v=15 m/s; additional processing time td=20 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要區間最小間距縮短全線運能必定同比提高」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Reducing open-line separation always increases whole-line capacity in the same proportion.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「班距監督與瓶頸」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Headway supervision and bottlenecks”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-01-k1","title":"班距監督與瓶頸","titleEn":"Headway supervision and bottlenecks","text":"本單元以月台占用和區間追蹤兩個資源比較班距，先找瓶頸再討論監督系統可調整的空間。班距是時間資源問題，不能僅用兩車車頭距離判斷。","textEn":"Compare platform occupation and open-line following as separate headway resources, identifying the bottleneck before considering what supervision can adjust. Headway is a time-resource problem, not merely a distance between train fronts.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要區間最小間距縮短全線運能必定同比提高 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Reducing open-line separation always increases whole-line capacity in the same proportion. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「班距監督與瓶頸」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Headway supervision and bottlenecks\" is correct?","options":["只要區間最小間距縮短全線運能必定同比提高","本單元以月台占用和區間追蹤兩個資源比較班距，先找瓶頸再討論監督系統可調整的空間。","同一段時刻餘裕可以同時完整吸收所有列車延誤"],"optionsEn":["Reducing open-line separation always increases whole-line capacity in the same proportion.","Compare platform occupation and open-line following as separate headway resources, identifying the bottleneck before considering what supervision can adjust.","The same timetable buffer can fully absorb every train delay simultaneously."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以月台占用和區間追蹤兩個資源比較班距，先找瓶頸再討論監督系統可調整的空間。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Compare platform occupation and open-line following as separate headway resources, identifying the bottleneck before considering what supervision can adjust. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b369-v16-02","title":"班距監督與瓶頸：定量估算","titleEn":"Headway supervision and bottlenecks: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「班距監督與瓶頸」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Headway supervision and bottlenecks” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：列車占用長度 L=180 m；假想防護距離 S=420 m；等速速度 v=15 m/s；附加處理時間 td=20 s。公式 y=(L+S)/v+td，代入得 y=60 s。邊界：等速單一資源的概念下界，不是任何號誌系統的實際最小班距。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: occupied train length L=180 m; hypothetical protected distance S=420 m; constant speed v=15 m/s; additional processing time td=20 s. Formula y=(L+S)/v+td gives y=60 s. Boundary: Conceptual lower bound for one resource at constant speed, not an operating minimum for any signalling system. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以時空圖標出車尾清空與資源釋放時刻，再檢查月台、道岔及折返各自的占用。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Mark rear clearance and resource release on a time-distance diagram, then examine platform, point and reversal occupation separately.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：列車占用長度 L=180 m；假想防護距離 S=420 m；等速速度 v=15 m/s；附加處理時間 td=20 s。公式 y=(L+S)/v+td，代入得 y=60 s。邊界：等速單一資源的概念下界，不是任何號誌系統的實際最小班距。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: occupied train length L=180 m; hypothetical protected distance S=420 m; constant speed v=15 m/s; additional processing time td=20 s. Formula y=(L+S)/v+td gives y=60 s. Boundary: Conceptual lower bound for one resource at constant speed, not an operating minimum for any signalling system.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「班距監督與瓶頸」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Headway supervision and bottlenecks\", which statement holds?","options":["出口每秒通過人數穩定就能證明站內沒有排隊","測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致","原創假想教學輸入：列車占用長度 L=180 m；假想防護距離 S=420 m；等速速度 v=15 m/s；附加處理時間 td=20 s。"],"optionsEn":["Stable exit throughput proves that no queue is forming inside the station.","Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: occupied train length L=180 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：列車占用長度 L=180 m；假想防護距離 S=420 m；等速速度 v=15 m/s；附加處理時間 td=20 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: occupied train length L=180 m; hypothetical protected distance S=420 m; constant speed v=15 m/s; additional processing time td=20 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b369-v16-03","title":"班距監督與瓶頸：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Headway supervision and bottlenecks: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「班距監督與瓶頸」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Headway supervision and bottlenecks” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以時空圖標出車尾清空與資源釋放時刻，再檢查月台、道岔及折返各自的占用。以「班距監督與瓶頸」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Mark rear clearance and resource release on a time-distance diagram, then examine platform, point and reversal occupation separately. For headway supervision and bottlenecks, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把假想防護距離 S 從 420 改成 462 m（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 60 變為 62.8 s。先說明「班距監督與瓶頸」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only hypothetical protected distance S from 420 to 462 m (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 60 to 62.8 s. Explain the causal direction for headway supervision and bottlenecks, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：將車頭離站當成月台路徑已清空會低估占用時間，瓶頸轉移則會造成局部改善卻全線延誤。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating front departure as complete route clearance understates occupation; a shifted bottleneck can improve one section while delays persist elsewhere. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以時空圖標出車尾清空與資源釋放時刻，再檢查月台、道岔及折返各自的占用。以「班距監督與瓶頸」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Mark rear clearance and resource release on a time-distance diagram, then examine platform, point and reversal occupation separately. For headway supervision and bottlenecks, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把假想防護距離 S 從 420 改成 462 m（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 60 變為 62.8 s。先說明「班距監督與瓶頸」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only hypothetical protected distance S from 420 to 462 m (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 60 to 62.8 s. Explain the causal direction for headway supervision and bottlenecks, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「班距監督與瓶頸」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Headway supervision and bottlenecks\"?","options":["以時空圖標出車尾清空與資源釋放時刻，再檢查月台、道岔及折返各自的占用。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合"],"optionsEn":["Mark rear clearance and resource release on a time-distance diagram, then examine platform, point and reversal occupation separately.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以時空圖標出車尾清空與資源釋放時刻，再檢查月台、道岔及折返各自的占用。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Mark rear clearance and resource release on a time-distance diagram, then examine platform, point and reversal occupation separately. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b369-v16-04","title":"班距監督與瓶頸：失效診斷","titleEn":"Headway supervision and bottlenecks: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「班距監督與瓶頸」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Headway supervision and bottlenecks” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將車頭離站當成月台路徑已清空會低估占用時間，瓶頸轉移則會造成局部改善卻全線延誤。回到「班距監督與瓶頸」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating front departure as complete route clearance understates occupation; a shifted bottleneck can improve one section while delays persist elsewhere. Trace the input chain for headway supervision and bottlenecks. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：等速單一資源的概念下界，不是任何號誌系統的實際最小班距。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Conceptual lower bound for one resource at constant speed, not an operating minimum for any signalling system.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要區間最小間距縮短全線運能必定同比提高」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Reducing open-line separation always increases whole-line capacity in the same proportion.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將車頭離站當成月台路徑已清空會低估占用時間，瓶頸轉移則會造成局部改善卻全線延誤。回到「班距監督與瓶頸」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Treating front departure as complete route clearance understates occupation; a shifted bottleneck can improve one section while delays persist elsewhere. Trace the input chain for headway supervision and bottlenecks. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「班距監督與瓶頸」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Headway supervision and bottlenecks\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","將車頭離站當成月台路徑已清空會低估占用時間，瓶頸轉移則會造成局部改善卻全線延誤。","同一段時刻餘裕可以同時完整吸收所有列車延誤"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Treating front departure as complete route clearance understates occupation; a shifted bottleneck can improve one section while delays persist elsewhere.","The same timetable buffer can fully absorb every train delay simultaneously."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將車頭離站當成月台路徑已清空會低估占用時間，瓶頸轉移則會造成局部改善卻全線延誤。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating front departure as complete route clearance understates occupation; a shifted bottleneck can improve one section while delays persist elsewhere. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b369-v16-05","title":"時刻偏差吸收：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Absorbing timetable deviation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-04"],"objective":"說明「時刻偏差吸收」如何影響列車自動監督系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Absorbing timetable deviation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Automatic train supervision systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元將提前、延誤與可用餘裕列在同一時空圖，防止同一段緩衝被多項調整重複使用。時刻表餘裕是已排間隔扣除占用與擾動後的剩餘時間。餘裕可以吸收小延誤，卻不是可隨意重複使用的免費容量；同一段緩衝若被兩個衝突約束同時借用，紙面上可行的時刻仍會在實際重播中互相追趕。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：單一衝突資源與確定延誤，未求解整個網路的隨機時刻最佳化。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「時刻偏差吸收」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Place early running, delay and available margin on one time-distance diagram so several adjustments cannot silently consume the same recovery buffer. Timetable margin is scheduled separation less occupation and perturbation. It can absorb small delays but is not free capacity that may be reused indefinitely. If two conflicting constraints both claim the same buffer, a timetable that appears feasible on paper can still produce converging delays in replay. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: One conflicting resource and a deterministic delay; no stochastic network-wide timetable optimization is implied. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Absorbing timetable deviation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：排定間隔 scheduled=140 s；資源占用 occupied=110 s；入侵延誤 delay=18 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: scheduled interval scheduled=140 s; resource occupation occupied=110 s; incoming delay delay=18 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「同一段時刻餘裕可以同時完整吸收所有列車延誤」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The same timetable buffer can fully absorb every train delay simultaneously.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「時刻偏差吸收」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Absorbing timetable deviation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-05-k1","title":"時刻偏差吸收","titleEn":"Absorbing timetable deviation","text":"本單元將提前、延誤與可用餘裕列在同一時空圖，防止同一段緩衝被多項調整重複使用。時刻表餘裕是已排間隔扣除占用與擾動後的剩餘時間。","textEn":"Place early running, delay and available margin on one time-distance diagram so several adjustments cannot silently consume the same recovery buffer. Timetable margin is scheduled separation less occupation and perturbation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：同一段時刻餘裕可以同時完整吸收所有列車延誤 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The same timetable buffer can fully absorb every train delay simultaneously. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「時刻偏差吸收」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Absorbing timetable deviation\" is correct?","options":["同一段時刻餘裕可以同時完整吸收所有列車延誤","總旅客數相同就代表每次停站時間一定相同","本單元將提前、延誤與可用餘裕列在同一時空圖，防止同一段緩衝被多項調整重複使用。"],"optionsEn":["The same timetable buffer can fully absorb every train delay simultaneously.","Equal total passenger counts always produce equal dwell times.","Place early running, delay and available margin on one time-distance diagram so several adjustments cannot silently consume the same recovery buffer."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元將提前、延誤與可用餘裕列在同一時空圖，防止同一段緩衝被多項調整重複使用。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Place early running, delay and available margin on one time-distance diagram so several adjustments cannot silently consume the same recovery buffer. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b369-v16-06","title":"時刻偏差吸收：定量估算","titleEn":"Absorbing timetable deviation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「時刻偏差吸收」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Absorbing timetable deviation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：排定間隔 scheduled=140 s；資源占用 occupied=110 s；入侵延誤 delay=18 s。公式 y=scheduled-occupied-delay，代入得 y=12 s。邊界：單一衝突資源與確定延誤，未求解整個網路的隨機時刻最佳化。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: scheduled interval scheduled=140 s; resource occupation occupied=110 s; incoming delay delay=18 s. Formula y=scheduled-occupied-delay gives y=12 s. Boundary: One conflicting resource and a deterministic delay; no stochastic network-wide timetable optimization is implied. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將每一段餘裕標記唯一用途，逐列重播延誤，檢查負餘裕是否傳到下一個路口。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Assign each buffer a unique purpose, replay train delays in sequence, and check whether negative margin propagates to the next junction.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：排定間隔 scheduled=140 s；資源占用 occupied=110 s；入侵延誤 delay=18 s。公式 y=scheduled-occupied-delay，代入得 y=12 s。邊界：單一衝突資源與確定延誤，未求解整個網路的隨機時刻最佳化。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: scheduled interval scheduled=140 s; resource occupation occupied=110 s; incoming delay delay=18 s. Formula y=scheduled-occupied-delay gives y=12 s. Boundary: One conflicting resource and a deterministic delay; no stochastic network-wide timetable optimization is implied.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「時刻偏差吸收」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Absorbing timetable deviation\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教學輸入：排定間隔 scheduled=140 s；資源占用 occupied=110 s；入侵延誤 delay=18 s。","平均頻寬足夠就保證每一個封包都準時抵達","操作員把所有警報點選確認就代表根本問題都已解決"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs: scheduled interval scheduled=140 s; resource occupation occupied=110 s; incoming delay delay=18 s.","Sufficient average bandwidth guarantees on-time arrival of every packet.","Acknowledging every alarm means that all underlying problems have been solved."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：排定間隔 scheduled=140 s；資源占用 occupied=110 s；入侵延誤 delay=18 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: scheduled interval scheduled=140 s; resource occupation occupied=110 s; incoming delay delay=18 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b369-v16-07","title":"時刻偏差吸收：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Absorbing timetable deviation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「時刻偏差吸收」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Absorbing timetable deviation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將每一段餘裕標記唯一用途，逐列重播延誤，檢查負餘裕是否傳到下一個路口。以「時刻偏差吸收」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Assign each buffer a unique purpose, replay train delays in sequence, and check whether negative margin propagates to the next junction. For absorbing timetable deviation, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把入侵延誤 delay 從 18 改成 19.8 s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 12 變為 10.2 s。先說明「時刻偏差吸收」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only incoming delay delay from 18 to 19.8 s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 12 to 10.2 s. Explain the causal direction for absorbing timetable deviation, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：重複計入同一緩衝會掩蓋衝突；把終點補時誤算為上游路口可用時間也會高估穩健度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Double-counted buffers hide conflicts; recovery time at a terminus cannot automatically be used at an earlier junction. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將每一段餘裕標記唯一用途，逐列重播延誤，檢查負餘裕是否傳到下一個路口。以「時刻偏差吸收」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Assign each buffer a unique purpose, replay train delays in sequence, and check whether negative margin propagates to the next junction. For absorbing timetable deviation, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把入侵延誤 delay 從 18 改成 19.8 s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 12 變為 10.2 s。先說明「時刻偏差吸收」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only incoming delay delay from 18 to 19.8 s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 12 to 10.2 s. Explain the causal direction for absorbing timetable deviation, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「時刻偏差吸收」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Absorbing timetable deviation\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將每一段餘裕標記唯一用途，逐列重播延誤，檢查負餘裕是否傳到下一個路口。","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Assign each buffer a unique purpose, replay train delays in sequence, and check whether negative margin propagates to the next junction.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將每一段餘裕標記唯一用途，逐列重播延誤，檢查負餘裕是否傳到下一個路口。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Assign each buffer a unique purpose, replay train delays in sequence, and check whether negative margin propagates to the next junction. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b369-v16-08","title":"時刻偏差吸收：失效診斷","titleEn":"Absorbing timetable deviation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「時刻偏差吸收」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Absorbing timetable deviation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"重複計入同一緩衝會掩蓋衝突；把終點補時誤算為上游路口可用時間也會高估穩健度。回到「時刻偏差吸收」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Double-counted buffers hide conflicts; recovery time at a terminus cannot automatically be used at an earlier junction. Trace the input chain for absorbing timetable deviation. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：單一衝突資源與確定延誤，未求解整個網路的隨機時刻最佳化。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: One conflicting resource and a deterministic delay; no stochastic network-wide timetable optimization is implied.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「同一段時刻餘裕可以同時完整吸收所有列車延誤」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The same timetable buffer can fully absorb every train delay simultaneously.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"重複計入同一緩衝會掩蓋衝突；把終點補時誤算為上游路口可用時間也會高估穩健度。回到「時刻偏差吸收」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Double-counted buffers hide conflicts; recovery time at a terminus cannot automatically be used at an earlier junction. Trace the input chain for absorbing timetable deviation. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「時刻偏差吸收」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Absorbing timetable deviation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","總旅客數相同就代表每次停站時間一定相同","重複計入同一緩衝會掩蓋衝突；把終點補時誤算為上游路口可用時間也會高估穩健度。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Equal total passenger counts always produce equal dwell times.","Double-counted buffers hide conflicts; recovery time at a terminus cannot automatically be used at an earlier junction."],"answer":2,"explanation":"重複計入同一緩衝會掩蓋衝突；把終點補時誤算為上游路口可用時間也會高估穩健度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Double-counted buffers hide conflicts; recovery time at a terminus cannot automatically be used at an earlier junction. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b369-v16-s2","title":"停站延長決策與旅客服務需求累積","titleEn":"Dwell-extension decisions & Accumulation of passenger service demand","description":"本階段聚焦「停站延長決策」與「旅客服務需求累積」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Dwell-extension decisions\" and \"Accumulation of passenger service demand\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b369-v16-09","title":"停站延長決策：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Dwell-extension decisions: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-08"],"objective":"說明「停站延長決策」如何影響列車自動監督系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Dwell-extension decisions” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Automatic train supervision systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元比較延長停站接續轉乘與保持後車間距的衝突，把旅客服務目標與線路容量一起呈現。停站時間包含人流服務與固定開關門程序。各門均分旅客時可用總服務率估算，但熱門樓梯旁的門通常更壅塞；瓶頸門完成時間控制發車，平均流率因此不能保證最忙車門也能按時結束。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：均勻單向登車，沒有下車逆流、行李阻塞或門重開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「停站延長決策」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Compare holding a train for connections with preserving separation from its follower, presenting passenger-service objectives alongside the route-capacity consequences. Dwell includes passenger service and fixed door sequences. Dividing by total service rate assumes an even passenger distribution, yet doors near popular stairs are often more crowded. The busiest door governs completion, so average flow cannot guarantee timely clearance at that door. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Uniform one-way boarding without alighting counterflow, luggage blockage or door reopening. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Dwell-extension decisions” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：登車人數 N=180 persons；有效門數 doors=12 doors；每門流率 rate=0.8 persons/(s*door)；固定程序時間 fixed=12 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: boarding passengers N=180 persons; effective doors doors=12 doors; flow per door rate=0.8 persons/(s*door); fixed procedure time fixed=12 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「總旅客數相同就代表每次停站時間一定相同」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal total passenger counts always produce equal dwell times.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「停站延長決策」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Dwell-extension decisions”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-09-k1","title":"停站延長決策","titleEn":"Dwell-extension decisions","text":"本單元比較延長停站接續轉乘與保持後車間距的衝突，把旅客服務目標與線路容量一起呈現。停站時間包含人流服務與固定開關門程序。","textEn":"Compare holding a train for connections with preserving separation from its follower, presenting passenger-service objectives alongside the route-capacity consequences. Dwell includes passenger service and fixed door sequences.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：總旅客數相同就代表每次停站時間一定相同 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal total passenger counts always produce equal dwell times. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「停站延長決策」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Dwell-extension decisions\" is correct?","options":["本單元比較延長停站接續轉乘與保持後車間距的衝突，把旅客服務目標與線路容量一起呈現。","總旅客數相同就代表每次停站時間一定相同","出口每秒通過人數穩定就能證明站內沒有排隊"],"optionsEn":["Compare holding a train for connections with preserving separation from its follower, presenting passenger-service objectives alongside the route-capacity consequences.","Equal total passenger counts always produce equal dwell times.","Stable exit throughput proves that no queue is forming inside the station."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元比較延長停站接續轉乘與保持後車間距的衝突，把旅客服務目標與線路容量一起呈現。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Compare holding a train for connections with preserving separation from its follower, presenting passenger-service objectives alongside the route-capacity consequences. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b369-v16-10","title":"停站延長決策：定量估算","titleEn":"Dwell-extension decisions: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「停站延長決策」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Dwell-extension decisions” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：登車人數 N=180 persons；有效門數 doors=12 doors；每門流率 rate=0.8 persons/(s*door)；固定程序時間 fixed=12 s。公式 y=N/(doors*rate)+fixed，代入得 y=30.75 s。邊界：均勻單向登車，沒有下車逆流、行李阻塞或門重開。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: boarding passengers N=180 persons; effective doors doors=12 doors; flow per door rate=0.8 persons/(s*door); fixed procedure time fixed=12 s. Formula y=N/(doors*rate)+fixed gives y=30.75 s. Boundary: Uniform one-way boarding without alighting counterflow, luggage blockage or door reopening. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：逐門記錄開始與結束時間，將固定程序從人流時間中扣除，再比較最忙門與平均門。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record start and finish at each door, subtract fixed procedure time, and compare the busiest door with the mean.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：登車人數 N=180 persons；有效門數 doors=12 doors；每門流率 rate=0.8 persons/(s*door)；固定程序時間 fixed=12 s。公式 y=N/(doors*rate)+fixed，代入得 y=30.75 s。邊界：均勻單向登車，沒有下車逆流、行李阻塞或門重開。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: boarding passengers N=180 persons; effective doors doors=12 doors; flow per door rate=0.8 persons/(s*door); fixed procedure time fixed=12 s. Formula y=N/(doors*rate)+fixed gives y=30.75 s. Boundary: Uniform one-way boarding without alighting counterflow, luggage blockage or door reopening.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「停站延長決策」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Dwell-extension decisions\", which statement holds?","options":["測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致","原創假想教學輸入：登車人數 N=180 persons。","狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合"],"optionsEn":["Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: boarding passengers N=180 persons.","Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：登車人數 N=180 persons；有效門數 doors=12 doors；每門流率 rate=0.8 persons/(s*door)；固定程序時間 fixed=12 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: boarding passengers N=180 persons; effective doors doors=12 doors; flow per door rate=0.8 persons/(s*door); fixed procedure time fixed=12 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b369-v16-11","title":"停站延長決策：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Dwell-extension decisions: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「停站延長決策」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Dwell-extension decisions” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"逐門記錄開始與結束時間，將固定程序從人流時間中扣除，再比較最忙門與平均門。以「停站延長決策」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record start and finish at each door, subtract fixed procedure time, and compare the busiest door with the mean. For dwell-extension decisions, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把登車人數 N 從 180 改成 181 persons（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 30.75 變為 30.8542 s。先說明「停站延長決策」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only boarding passengers N from 180 to 181 persons (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 30.75 to 30.8542 s. Explain the causal direction for dwell-extension decisions, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：平均人數正常但單門集中仍會延誤；門故障與旅客逆流都可能造成相似的總停站時間。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A normal average load can hide a concentrated door queue; mechanical faults and passenger counterflow can produce similar total dwell. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"逐門記錄開始與結束時間，將固定程序從人流時間中扣除，再比較最忙門與平均門。以「停站延長決策」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Record start and finish at each door, subtract fixed procedure time, and compare the busiest door with the mean. For dwell-extension decisions, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把登車人數 N 從 180 改成 181 persons（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 30.75 變為 30.8542 s。先說明「停站延長決策」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only boarding passengers N from 180 to 181 persons (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 30.75 to 30.8542 s. Explain the causal direction for dwell-extension decisions, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「停站延長決策」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Dwell-extension decisions\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","所有整合測試都可以同時執行而完全不影響結果","逐門記錄開始與結束時間，將固定程序從人流時間中扣除，再比較最忙門與平均門。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","All integration tests can run simultaneously without affecting results.","Record start and finish at each door, subtract fixed procedure time, and compare the busiest door with the mean."],"answer":2,"explanation":"逐門記錄開始與結束時間，將固定程序從人流時間中扣除，再比較最忙門與平均門。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record start and finish at each door, subtract fixed procedure time, and compare the busiest door with the mean. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b369-v16-12","title":"停站延長決策：失效診斷","titleEn":"Dwell-extension decisions: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「停站延長決策」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Dwell-extension decisions” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"平均人數正常但單門集中仍會延誤；門故障與旅客逆流都可能造成相似的總停站時間。回到「停站延長決策」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A normal average load can hide a concentrated door queue; mechanical faults and passenger counterflow can produce similar total dwell. Trace the input chain for dwell-extension decisions. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：均勻單向登車，沒有下車逆流、行李阻塞或門重開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Uniform one-way boarding without alighting counterflow, luggage blockage or door reopening.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「總旅客數相同就代表每次停站時間一定相同」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal total passenger counts always produce equal dwell times.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"平均人數正常但單門集中仍會延誤；門故障與旅客逆流都可能造成相似的總停站時間。回到「停站延長決策」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"A normal average load can hide a concentrated door queue; mechanical faults and passenger counterflow can produce similar total dwell. Trace the input chain for dwell-extension decisions. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「停站延長決策」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Dwell-extension decisions\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["平均人數正常但單門集中仍會延誤；門故障與旅客逆流都可能造成相似的總停站時間。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","出口每秒通過人數穩定就能證明站內沒有排隊"],"optionsEn":["A normal average load can hide a concentrated door queue; mechanical faults and passenger counterflow can produce similar total dwell.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Stable exit throughput proves that no queue is forming inside the station."],"answer":0,"explanation":"平均人數正常但單門集中仍會延誤；門故障與旅客逆流都可能造成相似的總停站時間。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A normal average load can hide a concentrated door queue; mechanical faults and passenger counterflow can produce similar total dwell. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b369-v16-13","title":"旅客服務需求累積：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Accumulation of passenger service demand: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-12"],"objective":"說明「旅客服務需求累積」如何影響列車自動監督系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Accumulation of passenger service demand” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Automatic train supervision systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元以旅客請求進出服務區的模型觀察需求累積，將未服務旅客保留在資料中而非刪除。排隊人數依流入減流出的守恆關係累積。平均服務能力若只略高於平均需求，瞬間車潮仍會形成等待；人群不能被無限壓縮，所以排隊長度會回堵上游樓梯或月台，改變原先假設的到達方式。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：固定流率、初始無排隊且流入大於流出；不含放棄、繞行及密度回饋。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「旅客服務需求累積」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Use passenger entry and exit from a service area to observe demand accumulation, retaining unserved travellers in the data instead of removing them. A queue accumulates according to inflow minus outflow. Even service capacity slightly above mean demand can be overwhelmed by a train-arrival pulse. People cannot be compressed indefinitely, so a growing queue can block upstream stairs or platforms and alter the assumed arrival process. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Constant flows, initially empty queue and inflow above outflow; abandonment, rerouting and density feedback are excluded. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Accumulation of passenger service demand” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：到達流率 arrival=3.2 persons/s；離開流率 service=2.6 persons/s；觀察時間 duration=120 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: arrival flow arrival=3.2 persons/s; departure flow service=2.6 persons/s; observation duration duration=120 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「出口每秒通過人數穩定就能證明站內沒有排隊」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Stable exit throughput proves that no queue is forming inside the station.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「旅客服務需求累積」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Accumulation of passenger service demand”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-13-k1","title":"旅客服務需求累積","titleEn":"Accumulation of passenger service demand","text":"本單元以旅客請求進出服務區的模型觀察需求累積，將未服務旅客保留在資料中而非刪除。排隊人數依流入減流出的守恆關係累積。","textEn":"Use passenger entry and exit from a service area to observe demand accumulation, retaining unserved travellers in the data instead of removing them. A queue accumulates according to inflow minus outflow.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：出口每秒通過人數穩定就能證明站內沒有排隊 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Stable exit throughput proves that no queue is forming inside the station. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「旅客服務需求累積」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Accumulation of passenger service demand\" is correct?","options":["出口每秒通過人數穩定就能證明站內沒有排隊","本單元以旅客請求進出服務區的模型觀察需求累積，將未服務旅客保留在資料中而非刪除。","平均頻寬足夠就保證每一個封包都準時抵達"],"optionsEn":["Stable exit throughput proves that no queue is forming inside the station.","Use passenger entry and exit from a service area to observe demand accumulation, retaining unserved travellers in the data instead of removing them.","Sufficient average bandwidth guarantees on-time arrival of every packet."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以旅客請求進出服務區的模型觀察需求累積，將未服務旅客保留在資料中而非刪除。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Use passenger entry and exit from a service area to observe demand accumulation, retaining unserved travellers in the data instead of removing them. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b369-v16-14","title":"旅客服務需求累積：定量估算","titleEn":"Accumulation of passenger service demand: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「旅客服務需求累積」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Accumulation of passenger service demand” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：到達流率 arrival=3.2 persons/s；離開流率 service=2.6 persons/s；觀察時間 duration=120 s。公式 y=(arrival-service)*duration，代入得 y=72 persons。邊界：固定流率、初始無排隊且流入大於流出；不含放棄、繞行及密度回饋。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: arrival flow arrival=3.2 persons/s; departure flow service=2.6 persons/s; observation duration duration=120 s. Formula y=(arrival-service)*duration gives y=72 persons. Boundary: Constant flows, initially empty queue and inflow above outflow; abandonment, rerouting and density feedback are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同時數進入、離開與區內存量，以影像匿名計數或人工抽樣核對人數守恆。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Count entries, exits and occupancy together, using anonymous image counts or manual samples to verify conservation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：到達流率 arrival=3.2 persons/s；離開流率 service=2.6 persons/s；觀察時間 duration=120 s。公式 y=(arrival-service)*duration，代入得 y=72 persons。邊界：固定流率、初始無排隊且流入大於流出；不含放棄、繞行及密度回饋。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: arrival flow arrival=3.2 persons/s; departure flow service=2.6 persons/s; observation duration duration=120 s. Formula y=(arrival-service)*duration gives y=72 persons. Boundary: Constant flows, initially empty queue and inflow above outflow; abandonment, rerouting and density feedback are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「旅客服務需求累積」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Accumulation of passenger service demand\", which statement holds?","options":["操作員把所有警報點選確認就代表根本問題都已解決","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","原創假想教學輸入：到達流率 arrival=3.2 persons/s。"],"optionsEn":["Acknowledging every alarm means that all underlying problems have been solved.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: arrival flow arrival=3.2 persons/s; departure flow service=2.6 persons/s; observation duration duration=120 s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：到達流率 arrival=3.2 persons/s；離開流率 service=2.6 persons/s；觀察時間 duration=120 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: arrival flow arrival=3.2 persons/s; departure flow service=2.6 persons/s; observation duration duration=120 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b369-v16-15","title":"旅客服務需求累積：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Accumulation of passenger service demand: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「旅客服務需求累積」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Accumulation of passenger service demand” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同時數進入、離開與區內存量，以影像匿名計數或人工抽樣核對人數守恆。以「旅客服務需求累積」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Count entries, exits and occupancy together, using anonymous image counts or manual samples to verify conservation. For accumulation of passenger service demand, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把觀察時間 duration 從 120 改成 132 s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 72 變為 79.2 persons。先說明「旅客服務需求累積」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only observation duration duration from 120 to 132 s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 72 to 79.2 persons. Explain the causal direction for accumulation of passenger service demand, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：只量出口通過量會看不到後方累積，感測器漏計還可能讓看似平衡的流率掩蓋真實回堵。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Exit throughput alone misses upstream accumulation; missed detections can hide real spillback behind apparently balanced flows. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同時數進入、離開與區內存量，以影像匿名計數或人工抽樣核對人數守恆。以「旅客服務需求累積」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Count entries, exits and occupancy together, using anonymous image counts or manual samples to verify conservation. For accumulation of passenger service demand, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把觀察時間 duration 從 120 改成 132 s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 72 變為 79.2 persons。先說明「旅客服務需求累積」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only observation duration duration from 120 to 132 s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 72 to 79.2 persons. Explain the causal direction for accumulation of passenger service demand, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「旅客服務需求累積」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Accumulation of passenger service demand\"?","options":["同時數進入、離開與區內存量，以影像匿名計數或人工抽樣核對人數守恆。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只要區間最小間距縮短全線運能必定同比提高"],"optionsEn":["Count entries, exits and occupancy together, using anonymous image counts or manual samples to verify conservation.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Reducing open-line separation always increases whole-line capacity in the same proportion."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同時數進入、離開與區內存量，以影像匿名計數或人工抽樣核對人數守恆。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Count entries, exits and occupancy together, using anonymous image counts or manual samples to verify conservation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b369-v16-16","title":"旅客服務需求累積：失效診斷","titleEn":"Accumulation of passenger service demand: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「旅客服務需求累積」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Accumulation of passenger service demand” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只量出口通過量會看不到後方累積，感測器漏計還可能讓看似平衡的流率掩蓋真實回堵。回到「旅客服務需求累積」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Exit throughput alone misses upstream accumulation; missed detections can hide real spillback behind apparently balanced flows. Trace the input chain for accumulation of passenger service demand. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：固定流率、初始無排隊且流入大於流出；不含放棄、繞行及密度回饋。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Constant flows, initially empty queue and inflow above outflow; abandonment, rerouting and density feedback are excluded.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「出口每秒通過人數穩定就能證明站內沒有排隊」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Stable exit throughput proves that no queue is forming inside the station.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只量出口通過量會看不到後方累積，感測器漏計還可能讓看似平衡的流率掩蓋真實回堵。回到「旅客服務需求累積」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Exit throughput alone misses upstream accumulation; missed detections can hide real spillback behind apparently balanced flows. Trace the input chain for accumulation of passenger service demand. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「旅客服務需求累積」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Accumulation of passenger service demand\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只量出口通過量會看不到後方累積，感測器漏計還可能讓看似平衡的流率掩蓋真實回堵。","平均頻寬足夠就保證每一個封包都準時抵達"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Exit throughput alone misses upstream accumulation; missed detections can hide real spillback behind apparently balanced flows.","Sufficient average bandwidth guarantees on-time arrival of every packet."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只量出口通過量會看不到後方累積，感測器漏計還可能讓看似平衡的流率掩蓋真實回堵。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Exit throughput alone misses upstream accumulation; missed detections can hide real spillback behind apparently balanced flows. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b369-v16-s3","title":"監督訊息頻寬與到發時間共同時基","titleEn":"Supervisory message bandwidth & Common timebase for arrivals","description":"本階段聚焦「監督訊息頻寬」與「到發時間共同時基」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Supervisory message bandwidth\" and \"Common timebase for arrivals\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b369-v16-17","title":"監督訊息頻寬：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Supervisory message bandwidth: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-16"],"objective":"說明「監督訊息頻寬」如何影響列車自動監督系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Supervisory message bandwidth” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Automatic train supervision systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元統計多列車位置與狀態更新的通訊需求，分別比較同步推送和錯開傳送造成的佇列。網路負載必須把列車數、更新頻率、封包長度及協定額外開銷一併計入。總位元率只是起點，同步突發、重送與頻道共享仍會改變排隊延遲；容量充足也不代表封包的截止時間一定可以滿足。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：均勻持續流量，不包含加密協商、重送尖峰或介質競爭。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「監督訊息頻寬」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Account for position and status updates from many trains, comparing the queueing effects of synchronized reports with deliberately staggered transmission. Network demand includes train count, update frequency, packet length and protocol overhead. Aggregate bit rate is only a starting point because synchronized bursts, retransmissions and channel sharing affect queues. Adequate average capacity does not guarantee that every packet meets its deadline. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Uniform sustained traffic; handshakes, retransmission bursts and medium contention are omitted. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Supervisory message bandwidth” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：列車數 trains=30 trains；每次訊息大小 bytes=240 bytes；更新頻率 rate=5 Hz；協定擴張倍率 overhead=1.6 1。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: train count trains=30 trains; message size bytes=240 bytes; update frequency rate=5 Hz; protocol overhead factor overhead=1.6 1.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均頻寬足夠就保證每一個封包都準時抵達」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Sufficient average bandwidth guarantees on-time arrival of every packet.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「監督訊息頻寬」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Supervisory message bandwidth”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-17-k1","title":"監督訊息頻寬","titleEn":"Supervisory message bandwidth","text":"本單元統計多列車位置與狀態更新的通訊需求，分別比較同步推送和錯開傳送造成的佇列。網路負載必須把列車數、更新頻率、封包長度及協定額外開銷一併計入。","textEn":"Account for position and status updates from many trains, comparing the queueing effects of synchronized reports with deliberately staggered transmission. Network demand includes train count, update frequency, packet length and protocol overhead.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均頻寬足夠就保證每一個封包都準時抵達 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Sufficient average bandwidth guarantees on-time arrival of every packet. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「監督訊息頻寬」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Supervisory message bandwidth\" is correct?","options":["平均頻寬足夠就保證每一個封包都準時抵達","測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致","本單元統計多列車位置與狀態更新的通訊需求，分別比較同步推送和錯開傳送造成的佇列。"],"optionsEn":["Sufficient average bandwidth guarantees on-time arrival of every packet.","Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day.","Account for position and status updates from many trains, comparing the queueing effects of synchronized reports with deliberately staggered transmission."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元統計多列車位置與狀態更新的通訊需求，分別比較同步推送和錯開傳送造成的佇列。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Account for position and status updates from many trains, comparing the queueing effects of synchronized reports with deliberately staggered transmission. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b369-v16-18","title":"監督訊息頻寬：定量估算","titleEn":"Supervisory message bandwidth: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「監督訊息頻寬」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Supervisory message bandwidth” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：列車數 trains=30 trains；每次訊息大小 bytes=240 bytes；更新頻率 rate=5 Hz；協定擴張倍率 overhead=1.6 1。公式 y=trains*bytes*8*rate*overhead/1000，代入得 y=460.8 kbit/s。邊界：均勻持續流量，不包含加密協商、重送尖峰或介質競爭。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: train count trains=30 trains; message size bytes=240 bytes; update frequency rate=5 Hz; protocol overhead factor overhead=1.6 1. Formula y=trains*bytes*8*rate*overhead/1000 gives y=460.8 kbit/s. Boundary: Uniform sustained traffic; handshakes, retransmission bursts and medium contention are omitted. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在封包擷取中核對實際線上長度，將同步與錯開更新兩種情境分別量測延遲。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check actual wire length in packet captures and compare delay for synchronized versus staggered updates.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：列車數 trains=30 trains；每次訊息大小 bytes=240 bytes；更新頻率 rate=5 Hz；協定擴張倍率 overhead=1.6 1。公式 y=trains*bytes*8*rate*overhead/1000，代入得 y=460.8 kbit/s。邊界：均勻持續流量，不包含加密協商、重送尖峰或介質競爭。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: train count trains=30 trains; message size bytes=240 bytes; update frequency rate=5 Hz; protocol overhead factor overhead=1.6 1. Formula y=trains*bytes*8*rate*overhead/1000 gives y=460.8 kbit/s. Boundary: Uniform sustained traffic; handshakes, retransmission bursts and medium contention are omitted.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「監督訊息頻寬」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Supervisory message bandwidth\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教學輸入：列車數 trains=30 trains。","狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合","所有整合測試都可以同時執行而完全不影響結果"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs: train count trains=30 trains.","Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination.","All integration tests can run simultaneously without affecting results."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：列車數 trains=30 trains；每次訊息大小 bytes=240 bytes；更新頻率 rate=5 Hz；協定擴張倍率 overhead=1.6 1。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: train count trains=30 trains; message size bytes=240 bytes; update frequency rate=5 Hz; protocol overhead factor overhead=1.6 1. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b369-v16-19","title":"監督訊息頻寬：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Supervisory message bandwidth: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「監督訊息頻寬」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Supervisory message bandwidth” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在封包擷取中核對實際線上長度，將同步與錯開更新兩種情境分別量測延遲。以「監督訊息頻寬」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check actual wire length in packet captures and compare delay for synchronized versus staggered updates. For supervisory message bandwidth, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把列車數 trains 從 30 改成 31 trains（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 460.8 變為 476.16 kbit/s。先說明「監督訊息頻寬」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only train count trains from 30 to 31 trains (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 460.8 to 476.16 kbit/s. Explain the causal direction for supervisory message bandwidth, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：只用應用資料長度估算會漏掉協定開銷，所有車同時更新又可能造成短時佇列爆滿。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Application payload length alone misses protocol overhead; simultaneous train updates can fill queues despite moderate mean traffic. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在封包擷取中核對實際線上長度，將同步與錯開更新兩種情境分別量測延遲。以「監督訊息頻寬」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Check actual wire length in packet captures and compare delay for synchronized versus staggered updates. For supervisory message bandwidth, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把列車數 trains 從 30 改成 31 trains（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 460.8 變為 476.16 kbit/s。先說明「監督訊息頻寬」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only train count trains from 30 to 31 trains (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 460.8 to 476.16 kbit/s. Explain the causal direction for supervisory message bandwidth, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「監督訊息頻寬」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Supervisory message bandwidth\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","在封包擷取中核對實際線上長度，將同步與錯開更新兩種情境分別量測延遲。","同一段時刻餘裕可以同時完整吸收所有列車延誤"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Check actual wire length in packet captures and compare delay for synchronized versus staggered updates.","The same timetable buffer can fully absorb every train delay simultaneously."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在封包擷取中核對實際線上長度，將同步與錯開更新兩種情境分別量測延遲。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check actual wire length in packet captures and compare delay for synchronized versus staggered updates. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b369-v16-20","title":"監督訊息頻寬：失效診斷","titleEn":"Supervisory message bandwidth: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「監督訊息頻寬」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Supervisory message bandwidth” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只用應用資料長度估算會漏掉協定開銷，所有車同時更新又可能造成短時佇列爆滿。回到「監督訊息頻寬」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Application payload length alone misses protocol overhead; simultaneous train updates can fill queues despite moderate mean traffic. Trace the input chain for supervisory message bandwidth. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：均勻持續流量，不包含加密協商、重送尖峰或介質競爭。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Uniform sustained traffic; handshakes, retransmission bursts and medium contention are omitted.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均頻寬足夠就保證每一個封包都準時抵達」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Sufficient average bandwidth guarantees on-time arrival of every packet.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只用應用資料長度估算會漏掉協定開銷，所有車同時更新又可能造成短時佇列爆滿。回到「監督訊息頻寬」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Application payload length alone misses protocol overhead; simultaneous train updates can fill queues despite moderate mean traffic. Trace the input chain for supervisory message bandwidth. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「監督訊息頻寬」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Supervisory message bandwidth\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致","只用應用資料長度估算會漏掉協定開銷，所有車同時更新又可能造成短時佇列爆滿。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day.","Application payload length alone misses protocol overhead; simultaneous train updates can fill queues despite moderate mean traffic."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只用應用資料長度估算會漏掉協定開銷，所有車同時更新又可能造成短時佇列爆滿。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Application payload length alone misses protocol overhead; simultaneous train updates can fill queues despite moderate mean traffic. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b369-v16-21","title":"到發時間共同時基：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Common timebase for arrivals: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-20"],"objective":"說明「到發時間共同時基」如何影響列車自動監督系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Common timebase for arrivals” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Automatic train supervision systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元檢查行控紀錄和車站資訊系統是否使用一致時間，避免把時鐘漂移解讀成準點率變化。時鐘頻率偏差會隨時間累積成時間差，校時瞬間的偏移與之不同。多系統事件排序若依不同時鐘，可能把因果順序顛倒；校時跳變又會使量測區間長度失真，所以需記錄時鐘品質與校正事件。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：固定頻率偏差的線性累積，忽略溫度漂移與校時伺服動態。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「到發時間共同時基」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Check whether control logs and station information share a consistent timebase, avoiding interpretation of clock drift as a change in punctuality. Clock frequency error accumulates into time offset and differs from initial synchronization offset. Ordering multisystem events on different clocks can reverse apparent causality. Synchronization jumps can distort interval lengths, so clock quality and correction events must be recorded. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Linear accumulation at fixed frequency offset; temperature drift and synchronization-servo dynamics are omitted. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Common timebase for arrivals” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：時鐘頻率偏差 drift=20 ppm；未校時期間 duration=3600 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: clock frequency offset drift=20 ppm; unsynchronized interval duration=3600 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「到發時間共同時基」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Common timebase for arrivals”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-21-k1","title":"到發時間共同時基","titleEn":"Common timebase for arrivals","text":"本單元檢查行控紀錄和車站資訊系統是否使用一致時間，避免把時鐘漂移解讀成準點率變化。時鐘頻率偏差會隨時間累積成時間差，校時瞬間的偏移與之不同。","textEn":"Check whether control logs and station information share a consistent timebase, avoiding interpretation of clock drift as a change in punctuality. Clock frequency error accumulates into time offset and differs from initial synchronization offset.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「到發時間共同時基」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Common timebase for arrivals\" is correct?","options":["本單元檢查行控紀錄和車站資訊系統是否使用一致時間，避免把時鐘漂移解讀成準點率變化。","測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致","操作員把所有警報點選確認就代表根本問題都已解決"],"optionsEn":["Check whether control logs and station information share a consistent timebase, avoiding interpretation of clock drift as a change in punctuality.","Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day.","Acknowledging every alarm means that all underlying problems have been solved."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元檢查行控紀錄和車站資訊系統是否使用一致時間，避免把時鐘漂移解讀成準點率變化。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Check whether control logs and station information share a consistent timebase, avoiding interpretation of clock drift as a change in punctuality. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b369-v16-22","title":"到發時間共同時基：定量估算","titleEn":"Common timebase for arrivals: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「到發時間共同時基」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Common timebase for arrivals” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：時鐘頻率偏差 drift=20 ppm；未校時期間 duration=3600 s。公式 y=drift*1e-6*duration，代入得 y=0.072 s。邊界：固定頻率偏差的線性累積，忽略溫度漂移與校時伺服動態。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: clock frequency offset drift=20 ppm; unsynchronized interval duration=3600 s. Formula y=drift*1e-6*duration gives y=0.072 s. Boundary: Linear accumulation at fixed frequency offset; temperature drift and synchronization-servo dynamics are omitted. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用獨立時間基準比較多個時刻的偏移，從斜率分辨頻率誤差與一次性跳變。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare offsets at several times against an independent reference, using slope to distinguish frequency error from a one-time jump.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：時鐘頻率偏差 drift=20 ppm；未校時期間 duration=3600 s。公式 y=drift*1e-6*duration，代入得 y=0.072 s。邊界：固定頻率偏差的線性累積，忽略溫度漂移與校時伺服動態。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: clock frequency offset drift=20 ppm; unsynchronized interval duration=3600 s. Formula y=drift*1e-6*duration gives y=0.072 s. Boundary: Linear accumulation at fixed frequency offset; temperature drift and synchronization-servo dynamics are omitted.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「到發時間共同時基」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Common timebase for arrivals\", which statement holds?","options":["測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","原創假想教學輸入：時鐘頻率偏差 drift=20 ppm；未校時期間 duration=3600 s。","只要區間最小間距縮短全線運能必定同比提高"],"optionsEn":["One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: clock frequency offset drift=20 ppm; unsynchronized interval duration=3600 s.","Reducing open-line separation always increases whole-line capacity in the same proportion."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：時鐘頻率偏差 drift=20 ppm；未校時期間 duration=3600 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: clock frequency offset drift=20 ppm; unsynchronized interval duration=3600 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b369-v16-23","title":"到發時間共同時基：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Common timebase for arrivals: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「到發時間共同時基」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Common timebase for arrivals” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用獨立時間基準比較多個時刻的偏移，從斜率分辨頻率誤差與一次性跳變。以「到發時間共同時基」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare offsets at several times against an independent reference, using slope to distinguish frequency error from a one-time jump. For common timebase for arrivals, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把未校時期間 duration 從 3600 改成 3960 s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.072 變為 0.0792 s。先說明「到發時間共同時基」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only unsynchronized interval duration from 3600 to 3960 s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.072 to 0.0792 s. Explain the causal direction for common timebase for arrivals, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：只對齊開始時刻卻忽略頻率漂移，會讓長測試中的事件逐漸錯位，並誤判通訊延遲。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Aligning only the initial instant leaves frequency drift uncorrected, progressively misaligning events and suggesting false network delay. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用獨立時間基準比較多個時刻的偏移，從斜率分辨頻率誤差與一次性跳變。以「到發時間共同時基」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Compare offsets at several times against an independent reference, using slope to distinguish frequency error from a one-time jump. For common timebase for arrivals, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把未校時期間 duration 從 3600 改成 3960 s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.072 變為 0.0792 s。先說明「到發時間共同時基」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only unsynchronized interval duration from 3600 to 3960 s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.072 to 0.0792 s. Explain the causal direction for common timebase for arrivals, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「到發時間共同時基」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Common timebase for arrivals\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","總旅客數相同就代表每次停站時間一定相同","用獨立時間基準比較多個時刻的偏移，從斜率分辨頻率誤差與一次性跳變。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Equal total passenger counts always produce equal dwell times.","Compare offsets at several times against an independent reference, using slope to distinguish frequency error from a one-time jump."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用獨立時間基準比較多個時刻的偏移，從斜率分辨頻率誤差與一次性跳變。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare offsets at several times against an independent reference, using slope to distinguish frequency error from a one-time jump. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b369-v16-24","title":"到發時間共同時基：失效診斷","titleEn":"Common timebase for arrivals: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「到發時間共同時基」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Common timebase for arrivals” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只對齊開始時刻卻忽略頻率漂移，會讓長測試中的事件逐漸錯位，並誤判通訊延遲。回到「到發時間共同時基」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Aligning only the initial instant leaves frequency drift uncorrected, progressively misaligning events and suggesting false network delay. Trace the input chain for common timebase for arrivals. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：固定頻率偏差的線性累積，忽略溫度漂移與校時伺服動態。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Linear accumulation at fixed frequency offset; temperature drift and synchronization-servo dynamics are omitted.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只對齊開始時刻卻忽略頻率漂移，會讓長測試中的事件逐漸錯位，並誤判通訊延遲。回到「到發時間共同時基」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Aligning only the initial instant leaves frequency drift uncorrected, progressively misaligning events and suggesting false network delay. Trace the input chain for common timebase for arrivals. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「到發時間共同時基」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Common timebase for arrivals\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只對齊開始時刻卻忽略頻率漂移，會讓長測試中的事件逐漸錯位，並誤判通訊延遲。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","操作員把所有警報點選確認就代表根本問題都已解決"],"optionsEn":["Aligning only the initial instant leaves frequency drift uncorrected, progressively misaligning events and suggesting false network delay.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Acknowledging every alarm means that all underlying problems have been solved."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只對齊開始時刻卻忽略頻率漂移，會讓長測試中的事件逐漸錯位，並誤判通訊延遲。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Aligning only the initial instant leaves frequency drift uncorrected, progressively misaligning events and suggesting false network delay. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b369-v16-s4","title":"營運異常警報排序與列車任務狀態管理","titleEn":"Ordering operational alarms & Managing train-mission states","description":"本階段聚焦「營運異常警報排序」與「列車任務狀態管理」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Ordering operational alarms\" and \"Managing train-mission states\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b369-v16-25","title":"營運異常警報排序：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ordering operational alarms: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-24"],"objective":"說明「營運異常警報排序」如何影響列車自動監督系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Ordering operational alarms” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Automatic train supervision systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元將重複延誤警報與真正不同的設備異常分開，讓操作員看見原因鏈而非只看警報數。警報到達率描述操作員接收訊息的負荷，但嚴重度、重複性與處置時間也決定可管理性。大量同根因警報可能淹沒最早的關鍵訊息；抑制重複訊號應保留可追溯性，不能以刪掉重要警報來美化數字。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：平均警報到達率，非人因可接受上限或人員能力評分。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「營運異常警報排序」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Separate duplicate delay alarms from distinct equipment anomalies so operators can understand the causal chain rather than merely the alarm count. Alarm arrival rate describes operator information load, while severity, repetition and action time determine manageability. Many alarms from one cause can obscure the first critical message. Duplicate suppression must preserve traceability rather than deleting important alarms to improve a metric. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Mean alarm arrival rate, not an acceptable human-factors limit or a rating of operator capability. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Ordering operational alarms” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：警報數 events=18 alarms；觀察期間 minutes=6 min。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: alarm count events=18 alarms; observation interval minutes=6 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「操作員把所有警報點選確認就代表根本問題都已解決」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Acknowledging every alarm means that all underlying problems have been solved.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「營運異常警報排序」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Ordering operational alarms”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-25-k1","title":"營運異常警報排序","titleEn":"Ordering operational alarms","text":"本單元將重複延誤警報與真正不同的設備異常分開，讓操作員看見原因鏈而非只看警報數。警報到達率描述操作員接收訊息的負荷，但嚴重度、重複性與處置時間也決定可管理性。","textEn":"Separate duplicate delay alarms from distinct equipment anomalies so operators can understand the causal chain rather than merely the alarm count. Alarm arrival rate describes operator information load, while severity, repetition and action time determine manageability.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：操作員把所有警報點選確認就代表根本問題都已解決 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Acknowledging every alarm means that all underlying problems have been solved. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「營運異常警報排序」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ordering operational alarms\" is correct?","options":["操作員把所有警報點選確認就代表根本問題都已解決","本單元將重複延誤警報與真正不同的設備異常分開，讓操作員看見原因鏈而非只看警報數。","狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合"],"optionsEn":["Acknowledging every alarm means that all underlying problems have been solved.","Separate duplicate delay alarms from distinct equipment anomalies so operators can understand the causal chain rather than merely the alarm count.","Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元將重複延誤警報與真正不同的設備異常分開，讓操作員看見原因鏈而非只看警報數。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Separate duplicate delay alarms from distinct equipment anomalies so operators can understand the causal chain rather than merely the alarm count. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b369-v16-26","title":"營運異常警報排序：定量估算","titleEn":"Ordering operational alarms: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「營運異常警報排序」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Ordering operational alarms” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：警報數 events=18 alarms；觀察期間 minutes=6 min。公式 y=events/minutes，代入得 y=3 alarms/min。邊界：平均警報到達率，非人因可接受上限或人員能力評分。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: alarm count events=18 alarms; observation interval minutes=6 min. Formula y=events/minutes gives y=3 alarms/min. Boundary: Mean alarm arrival rate, not an acceptable human-factors limit or a rating of operator capability. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以匿名情境重播記錄首個相關警報、確認與處置時刻，分開統計重複及獨立事件。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Replay anonymized scenarios, timestamp first relevant alarm, acknowledgement and action, and separate duplicates from independent events.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：警報數 events=18 alarms；觀察期間 minutes=6 min。公式 y=events/minutes，代入得 y=3 alarms/min。邊界：平均警報到達率，非人因可接受上限或人員能力評分。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: alarm count events=18 alarms; observation interval minutes=6 min. Formula y=events/minutes gives y=3 alarms/min. Boundary: Mean alarm arrival rate, not an acceptable human-factors limit or a rating of operator capability.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「營運異常警報排序」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ordering operational alarms\", which statement holds?","options":["所有整合測試都可以同時執行而完全不影響結果","同一段時刻餘裕可以同時完整吸收所有列車延誤","原創假想教學輸入：警報數 events=18 alarms；觀察期間 minutes=6 min。"],"optionsEn":["All integration tests can run simultaneously without affecting results.","The same timetable buffer can fully absorb every train delay simultaneously.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: alarm count events=18 alarms; observation interval minutes=6 min."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：警報數 events=18 alarms；觀察期間 minutes=6 min。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: alarm count events=18 alarms; observation interval minutes=6 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b369-v16-27","title":"營運異常警報排序：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ordering operational alarms: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「營運異常警報排序」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Ordering operational alarms” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以匿名情境重播記錄首個相關警報、確認與處置時刻，分開統計重複及獨立事件。以「營運異常警報排序」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Replay anonymized scenarios, timestamp first relevant alarm, acknowledgement and action, and separate duplicates from independent events. For ordering operational alarms, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把警報數 events 從 18 改成 19 alarms（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 3 變為 3.16667 alarms/min。先說明「營運異常警報排序」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only alarm count events from 18 to 19 alarms (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 3 to 3.16667 alarms/min. Explain the causal direction for ordering operational alarms, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：警報洪流可能使操作員確認了所有訊息卻未處理根因，缺乏優先順序又會延遲關鍵判斷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An alarm flood can lead to acknowledging messages without addressing causes; missing prioritization delays critical interpretation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以匿名情境重播記錄首個相關警報、確認與處置時刻，分開統計重複及獨立事件。以「營運異常警報排序」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Replay anonymized scenarios, timestamp first relevant alarm, acknowledgement and action, and separate duplicates from independent events. For ordering operational alarms, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把警報數 events 從 18 改成 19 alarms（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 3 變為 3.16667 alarms/min。先說明「營運異常警報排序」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only alarm count events from 18 to 19 alarms (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 3 to 3.16667 alarms/min. Explain the causal direction for ordering operational alarms, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「營運異常警報排序」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ordering operational alarms\"?","options":["以匿名情境重播記錄首個相關警報、確認與處置時刻，分開統計重複及獨立事件。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","出口每秒通過人數穩定就能證明站內沒有排隊"],"optionsEn":["Replay anonymized scenarios, timestamp first relevant alarm, acknowledgement and action, and separate duplicates from independent events.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Stable exit throughput proves that no queue is forming inside the station."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以匿名情境重播記錄首個相關警報、確認與處置時刻，分開統計重複及獨立事件。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Replay anonymized scenarios, timestamp first relevant alarm, acknowledgement and action, and separate duplicates from independent events. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b369-v16-28","title":"營運異常警報排序：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ordering operational alarms: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「營運異常警報排序」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Ordering operational alarms” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"警報洪流可能使操作員確認了所有訊息卻未處理根因，缺乏優先順序又會延遲關鍵判斷。回到「營運異常警報排序」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An alarm flood can lead to acknowledging messages without addressing causes; missing prioritization delays critical interpretation. Trace the input chain for ordering operational alarms. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：平均警報到達率，非人因可接受上限或人員能力評分。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Mean alarm arrival rate, not an acceptable human-factors limit or a rating of operator capability.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「操作員把所有警報點選確認就代表根本問題都已解決」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Acknowledging every alarm means that all underlying problems have been solved.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"警報洪流可能使操作員確認了所有訊息卻未處理根因，缺乏優先順序又會延遲關鍵判斷。回到「營運異常警報排序」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"An alarm flood can lead to acknowledging messages without addressing causes; missing prioritization delays critical interpretation. Trace the input chain for ordering operational alarms. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「營運異常警報排序」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ordering operational alarms\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","警報洪流可能使操作員確認了所有訊息卻未處理根因，缺乏優先順序又會延遲關鍵判斷。","狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","An alarm flood can lead to acknowledging messages without addressing causes; missing prioritization delays critical interpretation.","Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"警報洪流可能使操作員確認了所有訊息卻未處理根因，缺乏優先順序又會延遲關鍵判斷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An alarm flood can lead to acknowledging messages without addressing causes; missing prioritization delays critical interpretation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b369-v16-29","title":"列車任務狀態管理：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Managing train-mission states: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-28"],"objective":"說明「列車任務狀態管理」如何影響列車自動監督系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Managing train-mission states” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Automatic train supervision systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元列舉上線、停駛與任務交接的合法狀態，檢查同一列車是否被分配互斥任務。布林狀態組合隨變數個數指數成長，這說明逐一人工檢查很快失去效率。可達性約束能排除不可能組合，但刪除條件必須有證據；安全性質通常針對所有可達狀態，而非幾個畫面上看起來合理的狀態。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：未限制的布林笛卡兒積；實際可達狀態通常較少，但需另證明。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「列車任務狀態管理」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Enumerate valid entry, withdrawal and assignment states, checking whether one train has accidentally been allocated mutually incompatible missions. Boolean combinations grow exponentially with variable count, explaining why manual enumeration soon becomes ineffective. Reachability constraints can eliminate impossible combinations, but each exclusion needs justification. Safety properties normally concern every reachable state rather than a few states that look plausible on a display. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Unconstrained Boolean Cartesian product; actual reachability can be smaller but must be established separately. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Managing train-mission states” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：布林變數數量 bits=8 bits。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: number of Boolean state variables bits=8 bits.","failure":"常見誤解：「狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「列車任務狀態管理」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Managing train-mission states”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-29-k1","title":"列車任務狀態管理","titleEn":"Managing train-mission states","text":"本單元列舉上線、停駛與任務交接的合法狀態，檢查同一列車是否被分配互斥任務。布林狀態組合隨變數個數指數成長，這說明逐一人工檢查很快失去效率。","textEn":"Enumerate valid entry, withdrawal and assignment states, checking whether one train has accidentally been allocated mutually incompatible missions. Boolean combinations grow exponentially with variable count, explaining why manual enumeration soon becomes ineffective.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「列車任務狀態管理」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Managing train-mission states\" is correct?","options":["狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","本單元列舉上線、停駛與任務交接的合法狀態，檢查同一列車是否被分配互斥任務。"],"optionsEn":["Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","Enumerate valid entry, withdrawal and assignment states, checking whether one train has accidentally been allocated mutually incompatible missions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元列舉上線、停駛與任務交接的合法狀態，檢查同一列車是否被分配互斥任務。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Enumerate valid entry, withdrawal and assignment states, checking whether one train has accidentally been allocated mutually incompatible missions. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b369-v16-30","title":"列車任務狀態管理：定量估算","titleEn":"Managing train-mission states: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「列車任務狀態管理」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Managing train-mission states” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：布林變數數量 bits=8 bits。公式 y=2**bits，代入得 y=256 states。邊界：未限制的布林笛卡兒積；實際可達狀態通常較少，但需另證明。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: number of Boolean state variables bits=8 bits. Formula y=2**bits gives y=256 states. Boundary: Unconstrained Boolean Cartesian product; actual reachability can be smaller but must be established separately. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用小型模型列舉轉移，再與需求允許的轉移表比較，對被排除狀態留下理由。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Enumerate transitions in a small model, compare against the required transition table, and document reasons for excluded states.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：布林變數數量 bits=8 bits。公式 y=2**bits，代入得 y=256 states。邊界：未限制的布林笛卡兒積；實際可達狀態通常較少，但需另證明。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: number of Boolean state variables bits=8 bits. Formula y=2**bits gives y=256 states. Boundary: Unconstrained Boolean Cartesian product; actual reachability can be smaller but must be established separately.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「列車任務狀態管理」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Managing train-mission states\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教學輸入：布林變數數量 bits=8 bits。","只要區間最小間距縮短全線運能必定同比提高","總旅客數相同就代表每次停站時間一定相同"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs: number of Boolean state variables bits=8 bits.","Reducing open-line separation always increases whole-line capacity in the same proportion.","Equal total passenger counts always produce equal dwell times."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：布林變數數量 bits=8 bits。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: number of Boolean state variables bits=8 bits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b369-v16-31","title":"列車任務狀態管理：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Managing train-mission states: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「列車任務狀態管理」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Managing train-mission states” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用小型模型列舉轉移，再與需求允許的轉移表比較，對被排除狀態留下理由。以「列車任務狀態管理」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Enumerate transitions in a small model, compare against the required transition table, and document reasons for excluded states. For managing train-mission states, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把布林變數數量 bits 從 8 改成 9 bits（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 256 變為 512 states。先說明「列車任務狀態管理」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only number of Boolean state variables bits from 8 to 9 bits (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 256 to 512 states. Explain the causal direction for managing train-mission states, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：把感測器故障狀態預先刪掉會讓證明失去關鍵邊界，狀態抽象過粗也可能隱藏時序競爭。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Excluding sensor-fault states can remove the crucial boundary from a proof; overly coarse abstraction may hide timing races. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用小型模型列舉轉移，再與需求允許的轉移表比較，對被排除狀態留下理由。以「列車任務狀態管理」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Enumerate transitions in a small model, compare against the required transition table, and document reasons for excluded states. For managing train-mission states, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把布林變數數量 bits 從 8 改成 9 bits（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 256 變為 512 states。先說明「列車任務狀態管理」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only number of Boolean state variables bits from 8 to 9 bits (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 256 to 512 states. Explain the causal direction for managing train-mission states, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「列車任務狀態管理」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Managing train-mission states\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","用小型模型列舉轉移，再與需求允許的轉移表比較，對被排除狀態留下理由。","平均頻寬足夠就保證每一個封包都準時抵達"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Enumerate transitions in a small model, compare against the required transition table, and document reasons for excluded states.","Sufficient average bandwidth guarantees on-time arrival of every packet."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用小型模型列舉轉移，再與需求允許的轉移表比較，對被排除狀態留下理由。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Enumerate transitions in a small model, compare against the required transition table, and document reasons for excluded states. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b369-v16-32","title":"列車任務狀態管理：失效診斷","titleEn":"Managing train-mission states: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「列車任務狀態管理」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Managing train-mission states” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把感測器故障狀態預先刪掉會讓證明失去關鍵邊界，狀態抽象過粗也可能隱藏時序競爭。回到「列車任務狀態管理」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Excluding sensor-fault states can remove the crucial boundary from a proof; overly coarse abstraction may hide timing races. Trace the input chain for managing train-mission states. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：未限制的布林笛卡兒積；實際可達狀態通常較少，但需另證明。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Unconstrained Boolean Cartesian product; actual reachability can be smaller but must be established separately.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把感測器故障狀態預先刪掉會讓證明失去關鍵邊界，狀態抽象過粗也可能隱藏時序競爭。回到「列車任務狀態管理」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Excluding sensor-fault states can remove the crucial boundary from a proof; overly coarse abstraction may hide timing races. Trace the input chain for managing train-mission states. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「列車任務狀態管理」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Managing train-mission states\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","把感測器故障狀態預先刪掉會讓證明失去關鍵邊界，狀態抽象過粗也可能隱藏時序競爭。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","Excluding sensor-fault states can remove the crucial boundary from a proof; overly coarse abstraction may hide timing races."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把感測器故障狀態預先刪掉會讓證明失去關鍵邊界，狀態抽象過粗也可能隱藏時序競爭。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Excluding sensor-fault states can remove the crucial boundary from a proof; overly coarse abstraction may hide timing races. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b369-v16-s5","title":"旅客資訊一致性與監督整合重播計畫","titleEn":"Passenger-information consistency & Supervision integration replay plan","description":"本階段聚焦「旅客資訊一致性」與「監督整合重播計畫」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Passenger-information consistency\" and \"Supervision integration replay plan\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b369-v16-33","title":"旅客資訊一致性：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Passenger-information consistency: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-32"],"objective":"說明「旅客資訊一致性」如何影響列車自動監督系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Passenger-information consistency” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Automatic train supervision systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元把月台顯示、車內播報與行控排程連成案例矩陣，要求每項更新能追溯同一版本。測試覆蓋率只對已定義的分母有意義。需求、狀態、轉移與危害各有不同分母，執行很多正常案例仍可能漏掉罕見但重要的交接；同一案例重跑多次不會自動增加獨立需求的覆蓋。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：計數式已知案例覆蓋，不是失效機率或安全完整性量化。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「旅客資訊一致性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Connect platform displays, onboard announcements and control schedules in a case matrix, requiring each update to trace to one consistent version. Coverage is meaningful only relative to its defined denominator. Requirements, states, transitions and hazards have different denominators. Many normal cases can still omit a rare but important handoff, and repeating one case does not automatically cover additional independent requirements. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Count-based coverage of known cases, not a probability of failure or a safety-integrity measure. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Passenger-information consistency” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases.","failure":"常見誤解：「測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「旅客資訊一致性」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Passenger-information consistency”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-33-k1","title":"旅客資訊一致性","titleEn":"Passenger-information consistency","text":"本單元把月台顯示、車內播報與行控排程連成案例矩陣，要求每項更新能追溯同一版本。測試覆蓋率只對已定義的分母有意義。","textEn":"Connect platform displays, onboard announcements and control schedules in a case matrix, requiring each update to trace to one consistent version. Coverage is meaningful only relative to its defined denominator.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「旅客資訊一致性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Passenger-information consistency\" is correct?","options":["本單元把月台顯示、車內播報與行控排程連成案例矩陣，要求每項更新能追溯同一版本。","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","所有整合測試都可以同時執行而完全不影響結果"],"optionsEn":["Connect platform displays, onboard announcements and control schedules in a case matrix, requiring each update to trace to one consistent version.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","All integration tests can run simultaneously without affecting results."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元把月台顯示、車內播報與行控排程連成案例矩陣，要求每項更新能追溯同一版本。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Connect platform displays, onboard announcements and control schedules in a case matrix, requiring each update to trace to one consistent version. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b369-v16-34","title":"旅客資訊一致性：定量估算","titleEn":"Passenger-information consistency: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「旅客資訊一致性」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Passenger-information consistency” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。公式 y=tested/total，代入得 y=0.8 1。邊界：計數式已知案例覆蓋，不是失效機率或安全完整性量化。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases. Formula y=tested/total gives y=0.8 1. Boundary: Count-based coverage of known cases, not a probability of failure or a safety-integrity measure. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。公式 y=tested/total，代入得 y=0.8 1。邊界：計數式已知案例覆蓋，不是失效機率或安全完整性量化。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases. Formula y=tested/total gives y=0.8 1. Boundary: Count-based coverage of known cases, not a probability of failure or a safety-integrity measure.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「旅客資訊一致性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Passenger-information consistency\", which statement holds?","options":["同一段時刻餘裕可以同時完整吸收所有列車延誤","原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。","出口每秒通過人數穩定就能證明站內沒有排隊"],"optionsEn":["The same timetable buffer can fully absorb every train delay simultaneously.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases.","Stable exit throughput proves that no queue is forming inside the station."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b369-v16-35","title":"旅客資訊一致性：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Passenger-information consistency: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「旅客資訊一致性」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Passenger-information consistency” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。以「旅客資訊一致性」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence. For passenger-information consistency, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把已執行案例 tested 從 72 改成 73 cases（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.8 變為 0.811111 1。先說明「旅客資訊一致性」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only executed cases tested from 72 to 73 cases (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.8 to 0.811111 1. Explain the causal direction for passenger-information consistency, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。以「旅客資訊一致性」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence. For passenger-information consistency, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把已執行案例 tested 從 72 改成 73 cases（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.8 變為 0.811111 1。先說明「旅客資訊一致性」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only executed cases tested from 72 to 73 cases (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.8 to 0.811111 1. Explain the causal direction for passenger-information consistency, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「旅客資訊一致性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Passenger-information consistency\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致","建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day.","Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b369-v16-36","title":"旅客資訊一致性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Passenger-information consistency: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「旅客資訊一致性」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Passenger-information consistency” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。回到「旅客資訊一致性」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised. Trace the input chain for passenger-information consistency. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：計數式已知案例覆蓋，不是失效機率或安全完整性量化。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Count-based coverage of known cases, not a probability of failure or a safety-integrity measure.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。回到「旅客資訊一致性」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised. Trace the input chain for passenger-information consistency. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「旅客資訊一致性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Passenger-information consistency\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","所有整合測試都可以同時執行而完全不影響結果"],"optionsEn":["Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","All integration tests can run simultaneously without affecting results."],"answer":0,"explanation":"縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b369-v16-37","title":"監督整合重播計畫：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Supervision integration replay plan: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-36"],"objective":"說明「監督整合重播計畫」如何影響列車自動監督系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Supervision integration replay plan” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Automatic train supervision systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元安排整日營運事件的縮時重播，將重置環境、保存證據和異常重測納入測試工時。測試工時包含案例執行與環境設定、資料復原及證據整理。平行化只有在資源和狀態真正獨立時有效；把多個會修改同一狀態的測試同時執行，可能造成結果不可重現，表面節省時間卻增加診斷成本。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：確定平均案例時間的串行估算，未含故障重測與資源衝突。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「監督整合重播計畫」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Plan accelerated replay of a full operating day, including environment reset, evidence preservation and anomaly reruns in the test-effort budget. Test effort includes case execution, setup, state restoration and evidence handling. Parallelism helps only when resources and state are genuinely independent. Concurrent tests modifying one shared state can become irreproducible, apparently saving execution time while increasing diagnostic cost. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Serial estimate with deterministic mean case time; failure reruns and resource conflicts are excluded. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Supervision integration replay plan” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：測試案例數 cases=120 cases；平均案例時間 minutes=8 min/case；設定與恢復時間 setup=180 min。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: test cases cases=120 cases; mean case duration minutes=8 min/case; setup and recovery time setup=180 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「所有整合測試都可以同時執行而完全不影響結果」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"All integration tests can run simultaneously without affecting results.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「監督整合重播計畫」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Supervision integration replay plan”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-37-k1","title":"監督整合重播計畫","titleEn":"Supervision integration replay plan","text":"本單元安排整日營運事件的縮時重播，將重置環境、保存證據和異常重測納入測試工時。測試工時包含案例執行與環境設定、資料復原及證據整理。","textEn":"Plan accelerated replay of a full operating day, including environment reset, evidence preservation and anomaly reruns in the test-effort budget. Test effort includes case execution, setup, state restoration and evidence handling.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：所有整合測試都可以同時執行而完全不影響結果 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: All integration tests can run simultaneously without affecting results. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「監督整合重播計畫」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Supervision integration replay plan\" is correct?","options":["所有整合測試都可以同時執行而完全不影響結果","本單元安排整日營運事件的縮時重播，將重置環境、保存證據和異常重測納入測試工時。","只要區間最小間距縮短全線運能必定同比提高"],"optionsEn":["All integration tests can run simultaneously without affecting results.","Plan accelerated replay of a full operating day, including environment reset, evidence preservation and anomaly reruns in the test-effort budget.","Reducing open-line separation always increases whole-line capacity in the same proportion."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元安排整日營運事件的縮時重播，將重置環境、保存證據和異常重測納入測試工時。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Plan accelerated replay of a full operating day, including environment reset, evidence preservation and anomaly reruns in the test-effort budget. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b369-v16-38","title":"監督整合重播計畫：定量估算","titleEn":"Supervision integration replay plan: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「監督整合重播計畫」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Supervision integration replay plan” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：測試案例數 cases=120 cases；平均案例時間 minutes=8 min/case；設定與恢復時間 setup=180 min。公式 y=(cases*minutes+setup)/60，代入得 y=19 h。邊界：確定平均案例時間的串行估算，未含故障重測與資源衝突。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: test cases cases=120 cases; mean case duration minutes=8 min/case; setup and recovery time setup=180 min. Formula y=(cases*minutes+setup)/60 gives y=19 h. Boundary: Serial estimate with deterministic mean case time; failure reruns and resource conflicts are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：逐案記錄前置狀態、執行時間與復原時間，分開列出正常完成和失敗重測。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record preconditions, execution and restoration for every case, separating normal completion from failure reruns.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：測試案例數 cases=120 cases；平均案例時間 minutes=8 min/case；設定與恢復時間 setup=180 min。公式 y=(cases*minutes+setup)/60，代入得 y=19 h。邊界：確定平均案例時間的串行估算，未含故障重測與資源衝突。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: test cases cases=120 cases; mean case duration minutes=8 min/case; setup and recovery time setup=180 min. Formula y=(cases*minutes+setup)/60 gives y=19 h. Boundary: Serial estimate with deterministic mean case time; failure reruns and resource conflicts are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「監督整合重播計畫」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Supervision integration replay plan\", which statement holds?","options":["總旅客數相同就代表每次停站時間一定相同","平均頻寬足夠就保證每一個封包都準時抵達","原創假想教學輸入：測試案例數 cases=120 cases；平均案例時間 minutes=8 min/case；設定與恢復時間 setup=180 min。"],"optionsEn":["Equal total passenger counts always produce equal dwell times.","Sufficient average bandwidth guarantees on-time arrival of every packet.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: test cases cases=120 cases; mean case duration minutes=8 min/case; setup and recovery time setup=180 min."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：測試案例數 cases=120 cases；平均案例時間 minutes=8 min/case；設定與恢復時間 setup=180 min。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: test cases cases=120 cases; mean case duration minutes=8 min/case; setup and recovery time setup=180 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b369-v16-39","title":"監督整合重播計畫：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Supervision integration replay plan: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「監督整合重播計畫」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Supervision integration replay plan” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"逐案記錄前置狀態、執行時間與復原時間，分開列出正常完成和失敗重測。以「監督整合重播計畫」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record preconditions, execution and restoration for every case, separating normal completion from failure reruns. For supervision integration replay plan, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把測試案例數 cases 從 120 改成 121 cases（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 19 變為 19.1333 h。先說明「監督整合重播計畫」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only test cases cases from 120 to 121 cases (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 19 to 19.1333 h. Explain the causal direction for supervision integration replay plan, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：省略復原步驟會讓前案狀態污染後案，僅報告成功案例時間則低估總測試成本。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitted restoration contaminates later tests with earlier state; reporting only successful durations understates total effort. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"逐案記錄前置狀態、執行時間與復原時間，分開列出正常完成和失敗重測。以「監督整合重播計畫」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Record preconditions, execution and restoration for every case, separating normal completion from failure reruns. For supervision integration replay plan, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把測試案例數 cases 從 120 改成 121 cases（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 19 變為 19.1333 h。先說明「監督整合重播計畫」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only test cases cases from 120 to 121 cases (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 19 to 19.1333 h. Explain the causal direction for supervision integration replay plan, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「監督整合重播計畫」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Supervision integration replay plan\"?","options":["逐案記錄前置狀態、執行時間與復原時間，分開列出正常完成和失敗重測。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","操作員把所有警報點選確認就代表根本問題都已解決"],"optionsEn":["Record preconditions, execution and restoration for every case, separating normal completion from failure reruns.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Acknowledging every alarm means that all underlying problems have been solved."],"answer":0,"explanation":"逐案記錄前置狀態、執行時間與復原時間，分開列出正常完成和失敗重測。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record preconditions, execution and restoration for every case, separating normal completion from failure reruns. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b369-v16-40","title":"監督整合重播計畫：失效診斷","titleEn":"Supervision integration replay plan: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b369-v16-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「監督整合重播計畫」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Supervision integration replay plan” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"省略復原步驟會讓前案狀態污染後案，僅報告成功案例時間則低估總測試成本。回到「監督整合重播計畫」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitted restoration contaminates later tests with earlier state; reporting only successful durations understates total effort. Trace the input chain for supervision integration replay plan. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：確定平均案例時間的串行估算，未含故障重測與資源衝突。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Serial estimate with deterministic mean case time; failure reruns and resource conflicts are excluded.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「所有整合測試都可以同時執行而完全不影響結果」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"All integration tests can run simultaneously without affecting results.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b369-v16-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"省略復原步驟會讓前案狀態污染後案，僅報告成功案例時間則低估總測試成本。回到「監督整合重播計畫」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Omitted restoration contaminates later tests with earlier state; reporting only successful durations understates total effort. Trace the input chain for supervision integration replay plan. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b369-v16-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「監督整合重播計畫」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Supervision integration replay plan\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","省略復原步驟會讓前案狀態污染後案，僅報告成功案例時間則低估總測試成本。","只要區間最小間距縮短全線運能必定同比提高"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Omitted restoration contaminates later tests with earlier state; reporting only successful durations understates total effort.","Reducing open-line separation always increases whole-line capacity in the same proportion."],"answer":1,"explanation":"省略復原步驟會讓前案狀態污染後案，僅報告成功案例時間則低估總測試成本。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitted restoration contaminates later tests with earlier state; reporting only successful durations understates total effort. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"curriculumVersion":16,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000,"flowDiagram":"assets/diagrams/v16-b369-zh.svg","flowDiagramEn":"assets/diagrams/v16-b369-en.svg"}};
